// MEASURED RESIDUE (2026-09-28; measured with tools/probe.py against retail
// 0x0062CCE0, 551B).  This shape is 549B with 108 non-reloc diffs, first at
// +0x083, and EVERY [esp+K] displacement in it matches retail's exactly, so
// the frame layout is solved: sub esp,0x3c, ebp as the zero register, the
// inner node in B-0x44, the outer node in B-0x40, `srm` in B-0x38, `game` in
// B-0x30, `m` in B-0x2c, the BuddyInfo copy at B-0x28.
//
// R1 SOLVED.  The compare's length tail must be a named local tested in its
// own statement:
//     const int tail = len1 - len2;
//     if (tail != 0) return tail;
//     return 0;
// With `return len1 - len2;` MSVC folds the mismatch test away and emits
// `sub eax,edx; jne`; retail emits `sub eax,edx; cmp eax,ebp; jne`.  This
// spelling reproduces retail's redundant cmp and cuts 154 -> 108 diffs.  The
// matched precedent 0x004C4530 (DiplomacyBriefingUnicodeListFind.cpp) folds
// the same test over the same compare loop, so the two bodies genuinely
// compiled from differently spelled sources.
//
// R2 OPEN: 2 bytes, the last structural difference.  At +0x00d2 retail stores
// the PRE-dereference list pointer and dereferences it afterwards:
//     call [eax+0x98]      ; srm
//     mov [esp+0x20], eax  ; store srm            <- retail
//     mov eax, [eax]       ; srm->end()
//     mov ecx, [eax+8]     ; begin
//     cmp ecx, eax
//     mov [esp+0x14], ecx  ; srmIt
// and at +0x1b6 it re-derives the bound from that slot:
//     mov ecx, [esp+0x24]  ; srm
//     mov edx, [ecx]       ; *srm == srm->end()
// This shape instead caches the end node into the same slot, so the store
// lands after the dereference and the bound is read without the extra
// `mov edx,[ecx]`.  Writing the loop as `srmIt != srm->end()` does re-derive,
// but MSVC then keeps the inner node in ebp rather than B-0x44, shrinking the
// frame to 0x38 and reallocating every displacement (533B, 387 diffs).
// Roughly twenty source shapes were tried against this -- function-scope
// declarations, const pointers, a named set pointer, a named game pointer, a
// status local, a cached outer end, do/while, two independent reads of the
// list, const list references -- and the outcome is strictly bimodal: either
// this exact allocation with the cached end, or the 0x38 reallocation.  A
// third shape would have to keep the 0x3c frame while leaving the bound a
// deref of the srm slot, which MSVC 7.1 does not appear to offer.
//
// 2026-09-29 battery (+6 shapes, all disproved, probe-verified):
// - `const int diff` (mismatch local): byte-identical to this shape; const
//   restores the redundant cmp for the length tail but NOT for the mismatch
//   diff at +0x17d (retail `sub eax,edx; cmp eax,ebp; jne`, ours `sub; jne`).
// - diff declaration-split (`int diff;` at loop top, assigned in the
//   mismatch arm): identical bucket (108 diffs / shape 0.977).
// - inverted tail (`if (tail == 0) return 0; return tail;`): identical
//   bucket; also leaves ours' extra `je` at +0x183 (retail tests the tail
//   once via `sub; mov; cmp; jne`, ours double-tests via `sub; mov; je` +
//   `cmp; jne`).
// - srm declaration-split (`StagingRoomMap *srm; srm = call;` + deref
//   bound): 533B / 387 diffs, the 0x38 reallocation bucket.
// - reference alias (`StagingRoomMap &srm = *call;` + `srm.begin/end()`):
//   same 0x38 bucket, same bytes class as the split.
// - break-form inner loop (`for (it = begin(); ; ++it) if (it == end())
//   break;`): same 0x38 bucket.
// Bimodality now holds over ~26 shapes: every deref-bound spelling lands in
// the 0x38/node-in-ebp bucket, every cached-end spelling in this 0x3c
// bucket. R2 looks compiler-internal; next lever is not another spelling.
// (finish_measure rates this exact body 0.7967, equal to the kept score.
// banked 2026-09-28 as author-estimate 0.9 with the 6-shape battery above.)

